wati.sfw.summary.waystone_block=Named teleport node for the Waystone network. Player-placed Waystones may be private or public; natural Waystones begin dormant. Same-dimension travel costs 1–6 levels by distance and cross-dimension travel costs 6 levels.
wati.sfw.summary.waystone_item=Placeable Waystone used to create a named network node. Crafted with stone bricks, amethyst, obsidian and an Ender Pearl.
wati.sfw.summary.warp_stone=Reusable portable access to discovered Waystones. Uses the normal distance/dimension XP cost and gains a 30-second cooldown after a successful trip.
wati.sfw.summary.return_scroll=Consumable scroll that returns to the exact origin of the previous successful Waystones journey.
wati.sfw.summary.death_scroll=Recovery scroll granted after death. Returns to a safely resolved point near the latest death and is not consumed when no safe destination exists.
wati.sfw.summary.home_scroll=Consumable scroll that returns to the current valid bed or Respawn Anchor, or world spawn when no valid personal spawn exists.
wati.sfw.summary.teleport_pad=Direct linked A-to-B teleporter. The recipe produces two pads; linked pads cost no XP and use step-on activation with anti-bounce protection.
wati.sfw.summary.structure_wilderness=Rare Overworld wilderness structure containing a dormant natural Waystone.
wati.sfw.summary.structure_village=Overworld village-biased sanctuary containing a dormant natural Waystone selected to match the surrounding biome.

